Use withLocal for simple. For `addObservation`, local returns observation. Good.
`deleteObservation`, `clearMemory`, `fetchLatestConversation`, `createConversation`, `fetchConversationTree`, `setConversationHead`, `resolveApproval` withLocal fallback. For resolveApproval local fallback return `{ ok: true, id: approvalId }`? Could implement `bff.memory.resolveApproval`? BFF memory service doesn't have. Simpler local fallback returns `{ ok: true, id: approvalId }` but that's not real. Since BFF never emits approvals, okay but maybe misleading. Could throw BffError not_found? But main would toast. If no sidecar and approval somehow, better return `{ok:true,id}`. Fine.
`fetchChangelog`: leave sidecar-only? Hosted modal error; acceptable. Could fallback empty but not needed.
`fetchConnectorCatalog`/`fetchConnectors`: leave sidecar-only; Settings hides when sidecarReachable false. But boot still calls; errors state hidden. Fine.

