Wait — `streamChat` wraps the fetch in try/catch. `fetch` returns a Response with status 502 (ok is false). `throw await studioError(response)` throws StudioApiError. The catch block:
```
} catch (error) {
    if (error instanceof StudioApiError) {
      throw error;   // <-- rethrows StudioApiError immediately!
    }
    ...
    if (!isTransportFailure(error)) {
      throw error;
    }
    ...
}
```
The catch rethrows ALL `StudioApiError` before checking `isTransportFailure`! That's the bug. I need to check `isTransportFailure` first for StudioApiError too. Let me fix the catch block.

