The test is testing the wrong thing. `isTransportFailure` is meant to be called with actual errors thrown. Let me change the test to create real StudioApiError instances:
```
expect(isTransportFailure(new StudioApiError({ code: "internal", message: "x", retryable: false }, 502, false))).toBe(true);
expect(isTransportFailure(new StudioApiError({ code: "mcp_unreachable", message: "x", retryable: true }, 502, true))).toBe(false);
expect(isTransportFailure(new TypeError("failed to fetch"))).toBe(true);
```

